// AUTO-GENERATED — do not hand-edit.
//
// Tinos, subsetted, base64-encoded as TrueType. Used by the PDF download builder
// (src/lib/download-templates/pdf.tsx) in place of @react-pdf/renderer's built-in
// Times-Roman.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS: the built-in "standard 14" PDF fonts are AFM-metric fonts with
// no embedded glyph data, and their encoding drops or mangles characters this app
// routinely emits. Two confirmed failures on the built-in Times-Roman:
//   • the EURO SIGN rendered as a broken glyph — in FDI/investment copy that is
//     everywhere ("bilateral trade reaching EUR 858 million");
//   • CYRILLIC was silently corrupted into Latin gibberish ("Москва" -> ">A:20"),
//     which broke PDF downloads of Russian transcript translations outright
//     (Russian is one of TRANSLATION_LANGUAGES in src/lib/transcriptions.ts).
// Embedding a real TrueType font with the glyphs fixes both, and closes the whole
// class of silent-corruption bugs rather than the two symptoms we happened to hit.
//
// WHY TINOS: it is metrically compatible with Times New Roman — the face the
// client's own templates use — so the body copy keeps the same measure and page
// count it had on the built-in Times-Roman. Licensed under the SIL Open Font
// License 1.1 (see LICENSE-Tinos.txt beside this file), so it is redistributable.
//
// WHY BASE64 AND NOT A FILE: same reason as assets.ts — reading files from disk in
// a Vercel serverless function depends on build-time file tracing, and a font that
// silently fails to load would fall back to a broken glyph set. Font.register()
// accepts a base64 data URL, so this is self-contained and cannot fail to resolve.
//
// SUBSET COVERAGE (pyftsubset, kern + liga retained, hinting dropped):
//   Latin-1, Latin Extended-A/B/Additional (European + Romanian + Turkish +
//   Vietnamese), combining marks, Greek, Cyrillic + supplement, General
//   Punctuation (dashes, curly quotes, ellipsis, bullets), super/subscripts,
//   Currency Symbols (EUR GBP RUB INR TRY UAH ...), Letterlike, Number Forms,
//   Arrows, Math Operators, Geometric Shapes, fi/fl ligatures.
//   NOT covered: CJK, Arabic, Hebrew, Thai, Devanagari — a font with those runs to
//   megabytes. Body copy in those scripts will not render; the Economic Observer
//   band's Chinese is baked into its JPEG, so that template is unaffected.
//
// To regenerate: re-subset the four Tinos TTFs over the ranges above and rebuild
// this file; keep all four styles, since pdf.tsx maps bold/italic onto them.

